      "text": "Always talking shit of America and homeless people. These are addicts!\n\nHomelessness doesn't create an addict, but addicts create Homelessness. \n\nMajority of homeless people aren't addicts living on a sidewalk. Addicts don't care where they live. They care about being high. \n\nThey get more help looking like shit stains then if they were cleaned up. They'd showed how much less help they get once you shower, shave and get them clothes. \n\nThey act like America is a homeless creation place. Less than .1% of the population is homeless and even less of that population lives in sidewalks! \n\nGiving them housing doesn't fix their issues you need to help them off drugs first. \n\nMost people don't even know anyone who is homeless. I've been homeless for years and never used drugs. I've had friends who did do drugs and are homeless. \n\nThis is the biggest issue. The common person don't know anyone homeless. So the homeless they think of is often addicts who make income from being dirty and begging.\n\nIf you care so much then why you don't get homeless friends? Are you too good? You'll feed them for praise, but you won't pull up a chair or tent and hang out to get to see what you don't see when watching stupid YouTube videos about homeless people!",
